  "style": {
    "name": "classical temple",
    "rationale": "A hexastyle peripteral temple in the Greek/Roman tradition: a three-tier crepidoma rising to a smooth-quartz stylobate, a full surrounding colonnade of fluted quartz-pillar columns on bases and chiseled capitals, a deep columned portico reached by a grand central staircase, a banded entablature (architrave, gold-triglyph frieze, overhanging crown cornice), a tall triangular pediment with a raking cornice and gilded tympanum over the entrance, and an enclosed cella sheltering a golden idol on a stepped altar beneath a coffered, sea-lantern-lit ceiling. White quartz reads as marble, tan sandstone grounds the base, gold and diorite give accent and shadow, and sea lanterns supply sacred light. Strict left-right (x) bilateral symmetry organizes the whole."
  },
